; modules/cascade-kingdom/module.ahk

WHY
=

Sometimes, I want my windows large, organized and easy to switch between.
=

ADD A WINDOW
=

Press Caps + Insert to add the active window, and Caps + Shift + Insert to take it out again: it returns to where it was before it joined.
=

Or hold Caps and double-click anywhere on a window to add it, and double-click it again to take it out, back to where it was.
=

While Caps is held, clicks only focus windows and never reach what is inside them.
=

Cascaded windows will get sorted automatically so the cascade stays compact and tidy.
=

MOVE A WINDOW
=

Dragging a window in a cascade shows corner guides on the available slots. The bigger guide is the slot it will take.
=

It swaps with the window there instead of sliding back into its own place.
=

Release with no guide lit to take the window out of the cascade; it stays where you dropped it, at the size it had before it joined.
=

Resizing a window by any edge also takes it out of the cascade, keeping its new size and place.
=

FOCUS TABS
=

Each slot has a focus tab on both sides: at the lower left and the upper right.
=

Click either to select a slot.
=

Click again to cycle windows sharing that slot (if your cascade has multiple layers of windows).
=

Active tabs and drop guides use your Windows accent color; choose the inactive tab color in Settings.
=

# nroj95's FAVORITE HOTKEY
=

Caps + M hides the cascade on your display when you're not using it; Caps + Shift + M brings it back.
=

; modules/paper-pad/module.ahk

Inspired by Yakuake, the drop-down terminal on Linux, I wanted a similar drawer for notes: somewhere to jot things down without digging through windows and tabs.
=

YOUR OWN QUICK-NOTES DRAWER
=

Paper Pad uses a dedicated Notepad3 window that stays on top while open and out of the way when hidden.
=

Make it appear with Win + F12 and press again to hide it.
=

Ctrl + N creates a new timestamped page.
=

Move back and forth between your pages with Win + Left/Right.
=

Page navigation shortcuts work only inside the editor.
=

SAVING AND SETTINGS
=

Paper Pad automatically saves changes when switching pages or hiding the drawer.
=

Settings lets you choose your Notepad3 executable, notes folder, display and drawer size.
=

; modules/power-up-utilities/power-up-utilities.ahk

Practical shortcuts for everyday tasks that don't fit into the other modules.
=

STAY AWAKE
=

Pause + End keeps the computer awake for 30 minutes, then puts it to sleep once you're no longer using it.
=

Press again while its notice shows for 1, 2, 4 or 8 hours or no limit.
=

Pause + Shift + End cancels it.
=

Pause + Pause shows how long is left.
=

For more reliable sleep, turn off Windows' Away Mode and let only your keyboard wake the computer.
=

MORE KEYS WITHOUT A NEW KEYBOARD
=

Caps + QWER/ASDF/ZXCV sends F13–F24; Caps + 0–9 provides a virtual number pad, even if your keyboard lacks those keys.
=

HANDY EXTRAS
=

Insert symbols such as ’, – or ß, the HTML entity &nbsp; or a timestamp such as 20261110-203729.
=

Terminal copy and clear operate only in Windows Terminal and use its default Ctrl + Shift + A, C and K shortcuts.
=

